          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"native-ibp-and-finite-terms\">Native IBP and finite terms</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The parametric recurrence and bounded Laporta reduction agree for <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(I_2||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(I_3||)</marimo-tex>, where <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(I_n=\\int_k(k^2-M+i0)^{-n}||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(I_1=A_0(M)||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Expand the dimension-dependent coefficients before removing the master pole. In particular, the factor <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D-4||)</marimo-tex> in <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(I_3||)</marimo-tex> multiplies the tadpole's <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex> pole and produces a nonzero finite triangle. The generic-momentum bubble separately checks that the UV pole has no <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2||)</marimo-tex> dependence.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
